2
00:00:37.522 --> 00:00:40.202
So, my approach with nutrition science

3
00:00:40.202 --> 00:00:44.043
has always been to let the science do the talking

4
00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:49.043 line:15%
and be led by the data or be open to changing your mind.

5
00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.865
(upbeat music)

6
00:01:09.465 --> 00:01:13.902
Very few topics are more hotly debated than nutrition.

7
00:01:13.902 --> 00:01:18.429
It truly is right up there with politics and religion,

8
00:01:18.429 --> 00:01:21.691
but the irony is that in terms of the optimal diet

9
00:01:21.691 --> 00:01:24.809
that considers both human and planetary health,

10
00:01:24.809 --> 00:01:28.658
the hard science is actually quite clear that we should

11
00:01:28.658 --> 00:01:31.577
and actually must be moving towards a diet

12
00:01:31.577 --> 00:01:35.170
that is as plant-exclusive as possible.

13
00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:38.130
Nonetheless, misinformation persists,

14
00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:41.792
confusing and paralyzing the average well-intentioned person

15
00:01:41.792 --> 00:01:46.515
which can and often does lead to avoidable disease.

16
00:01:46.515 --> 00:01:48.827
To help us today parse facts from fiction

17
00:01:48.827 --> 00:01:52.549
and guide us towards a reasoned, rational model

18
00:01:52.549 --> 00:01:54.983
for nutritional health and well-being,

19
00:01:54.983 --> 00:01:57.826
we convene with my friend, Simon Hill.

20
00:01:57.826 --> 00:02:01.001
Simon is the host of the fantastic Plant Proof Podcast

21
00:02:01.001 --> 00:02:02.910
and blog of the same name,

22
00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.648
both absolutely incredible resources

23
00:02:05.648 --> 00:02:08.073
and he plies his master's degree in nutrition

24
00:02:08.073 --> 00:02:11.595
to objectively decipher the scientific literature

25
00:02:11.595 --> 00:02:14.779
to help people make better diet and lifestyle choices

26
00:02:14.779 --> 00:02:18.302
to promote optimal health and longevity.

27
00:02:18.302 --> 00:02:20.131
Simon is also the plant-based food contributor

28
00:02:20.131 --> 00:02:22.538
to Chris Hemsworth's fitness app center

29
00:02:22.538 --> 00:02:25.606
and he's the author of this fantastic new book,

30
00:02:25.606 --> 00:02:27.828
"The Proof Is In The Plants"

31
00:02:27.828 --> 00:02:30.706
which is a phenomenal, evidence-based primer

32
00:02:30.706 --> 00:02:33.955
on the positive impact of a plant-predominant diet.

33
00:02:33.955 --> 00:02:37.717
We have all the hot topics today, tribal diet wars,

34
00:02:37.717 --> 00:02:40.293
what the science says, what it doesn't,

35
00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:43.223
the environmental implications of our food choices,

36
00:02:43.223 --> 00:02:47.675
the truth about saturated fat, cholesterol and seed oils

37
00:02:47.675 --> 00:02:50.309
and the key things you can and should be doing right now

38
00:02:50.309 --> 00:02:53.201
to perform at your peak, sidestep disease,

39
00:02:53.201 --> 00:02:58.155
promote longevity and live both optimally and consciously.

40
00:02:58.155 --> 00:02:59.495
For so many reasons,

41
00:02:59.495 --> 00:03:01.994
Simon is the health and nutrition resource

42
00:03:01.994 --> 00:03:06.155
we all need right now and this one is packed with crucial,

43
00:03:06.155 --> 00:03:08.354
perhaps even life-saving information,

44
00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:11.421
including links that Simon has provided to all the studies

45
00:03:11.421 --> 00:03:13.961
that he references throughout the conversation,

46
00:03:13.961 --> 00:03:16.358
which you can find in the show notes on the episode page

47
00:03:16.358 --> 00:03:17.818
at richroll.com.

48
00:03:17.818 --> 00:03:19.262
So, with that being said,

49
00:03:19.262 --> 00:03:23.012
please enjoy my conversation with Simon Hill.

50
00:03:24.379 --> 00:03:27.251
Mate, how long have we talked about doing this?

51
00:03:27.251 --> 00:03:28.084
It's been a long time.

52
00:03:28.084 --> 00:03:31.485
It has been a long time, years in fact.

53
00:03:31.485 --> 00:03:32.318
I know, it's--

54
00:03:32.318 --> 00:03:33.448
I was in Australia,

55
00:03:33.448 --> 00:03:35.798
I was tempted to do it with you then,

56
00:03:35.798 --> 00:03:37.470
I've been on your show a bunch of times,

57
00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:40.818
we've been friends for a couple of years at this point.

58
00:03:40.818 --> 00:03:43.769
I think I reached out to you to do this earlier,

59
00:03:43.769 --> 00:03:45.412
